iguration that requires the other member's vote; the harness did not read the restarted node's configuration \\\"\n        \\\"back, so that explanation is inferred rather than observed.\\\")\nassert old_ce in new['counterevidence']\nnew['counterevidence']=[new_ce if c==old_ce else c for c in new['counterevidence']]\nnew['counterevidence']=new['counterevidence']+[(\\\"The restarted node retained the lone commit in its own log while the peer still lacked it for the whole ten-second window, so the entry remained \\\"\n  \\\"unsupported by a quorum of the committed configuration after restart; whether it would eventually reach the peer once the node led again was not observed.\\\")]\nold_lim=(\\\"Restart behaviour, which is where the log-derived configuration would replace the phantom one, was not exercised, so nothing is claimed about recovery from this state.\\\")\nnew_lim=(\\\"Only one restart was observed: the node came back with the commit retained but did not regain leadership within ten seconds, and the reason it did \\\"\n         \\\"not lead was not diagnosed, so recovery after a restart remains open.\\\")\nassert old_lim in new['limitations']\nnew['limitations']=[new_lim if l==old_lim else l for l in new['limitations']]\nnew['joint_history']=(\\\"Receipt 76bdaf3e107643d4a3ed1247faa52460 is the successor of 6491640ed49a4c7b8f5150438d350e36-experiment under this question: the same cases and \\\"\n  \\\"admissions plus a restart phase. The two receipts agree on the failed change, the phantom configuration and the lone commit, so they describe the same \\\"\n  \\\"subject; the successor adds what a restart does to that state.\\\")\njson.dump({'rationale':(\\\"Fold the restart receipt into the phantom-configuration account: the lone commit was retained in the node's log, the peer stayed at index 2, \\\"\n  \\\"and the restarted node did not lead again within ten seconds. The earlier unexercised-restart limitation is replaced by that observation, the memory-only \\\"\n  \\\"counterevidence is narrowed to an inferred explanation, and a new counterevidence item records that the entry stayed unsupported after restart.\\\"),\n 'interpretations':[new]},open('draft/update.json','w'),indent=2)\nprint('ce',len(new['counterevidence']),'lim',len(new['limitations']))\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
